keel (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The package now ships a first boot hook,
    /usr/lib/inithooks/firstboot.d/10keel-system, which converges the system
    state the instance description declares by running "keel spec apply
    --system-only". It is numbered to run after 09hostname, whose sed over
    the old name would otherwise edit or lose the /etc/hosts entry, and
    before the hooks at 15, 29 and 30 that depend on the fully qualified
    name. The package that owns the keel command owns the hook that runs it,
    so inithooks needs no dependency on keel and an image without keel has
    no hook there. The hook is a no-op with exit 0 where there is no
    description, under turnkey-init, and where the description declares
    nothing that phase converges; it logs through the inithooks log and
    never aborts a boot for a failure it cannot fix.
  * keel spec apply gains --system-only, the system phase without the conf
    phase: no secret is resolved, so a generated password the earlier hooks
    already applied is never regenerated.

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 21:46:05 +0000

keel (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: the instance spec (load, validate, render, apply) and
    the keel command line interface. inspect, diff and verify are stubs.

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Wed, 24 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
